Correct the dashboard details reported after the first pass.

The header's settings button is dropped: this session's Wayle configuration
is declared in Home Manager, so anything the settings app writes is replaced
on the next rebuild. Do Not Disturb moves up beside the notification card's
title, which also gives the card back a row.

A notification's title now wraps to the same two lines the body already used
and the chevron expands both, so a long summary is no longer cut off however
often it is pressed. The chevron is offered for a long summary even when there
is no body, since a GTK label only reports that it is ellipsized after it has
been laid out.

The calendar puts an event's time on its own line above the event, split off
the `"<title> HH:MM-HH:MM"` label `waybar-ycal` caches, and the agenda is given
more room between its lines.

Every card title is drawn in the palette's red, the colour the calendar's date
range already used.

